{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1088 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0a6e09c735f3daf504d24b73b3b7a9cad4b5df24185bba92c9cdcd593e5ace0f" :edb/db-before-t 1087 :edb/db-after-t 1088 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534400 50 #inst "2026-10-07T00:20:28.299Z" 13194139534400 true] [17592186054590 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286385 13194139534400 true] [17592186054759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286376 13194139534400 true] [17592186054760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286363 13194139534400 true] [17592186054760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186286380 13194139534400 true] [17592186055054 1017 #edb/ref 17592186052108 13194139534400 false] [17592186055054 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286370 13194139534400 true] [17592186055054 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534400 true] [17592186055054 1100 "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)=2x.$" 13194139534400 true] [17592186055054 1100 "Calculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for $x\\ln y = 2x$." 13194139534400 false] [17592186055054 1145 "First, we differentiate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\nNote that to differentiate the $x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ term, we will need to use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y) & =2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\ [(x)(\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{dy}}{\\text{d}x})+(1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y))] & =2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we solve the equation for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y) & =2 \\\\ \\frac{x}{y}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y(2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y))}{x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286363 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286364 13194139534400 true] [17592186286363 1089 "q-14680" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286363 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534400 true] [17592186286363 1100 "The equation of a curve is $2{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}=8.$ The tangent line at the point $(1,\\,1)$ on the curve intersects the $y$-axis at the point $P.$ What are the coordinates of $P?$" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286363 1113 #uuid "e11c8036-c7f9-5f36-af42-ea8dbcd9d81a" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286363 1145 "First of all, we need to find the slope of the tangent line at the point $(1,\\,1).$  \n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we will calculate the derivative using implicit differentiation, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 4x+12y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 12y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{12y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,1)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}_{(1,\\,1)} \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{x}{3y})}_{(1,\\,1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can write the equation of the tangent at the point $(1,1)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-{y}_{1}) & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ (y-1) & =-\\frac{1}{3}(x-1) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3}(x-1)+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to find where this tangent line intersects the $y$-axis. At the point $P$ the $x$-coordinate is $0,$ so we set $x=0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{3}(x-1)+1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3}(0-1)+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,\\,\\frac{4}{3}).$" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286365 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286366 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286367 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286368 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286369 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1041 "selection" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286368 13194139534400 true] [17592186286364 1110 #uuid "bc81dd60-8bf1-5bcd-ba31-07b1c6bdffb4" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286365 1034 "(0,\\,-\\frac{4}{3})" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286365 1111 #uuid "16f43359-c122-54be-8d77-4bb4267b5859" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286366 1034 "(0,\\,\\frac{1}{3})" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286366 1111 #uuid "723ef586-19db-5f1f-9401-00c82807fbc1" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286367 1034 "(0,\\,2)" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286367 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286367 1111 #uuid "b168ca86-8ccb-5432-8645-a79cad4f817e" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286368 1034 "(0,\\,\\frac{4}{3})" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286368 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286368 1111 #uuid "917a34d0-4e26-59b9-b37c-dcd906042c84" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286369 1034 "(0,\\,-\\frac{1}{3})" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286369 1111 #uuid "15eab90f-310c-5d6f-83fd-1ec9c2cf5af9" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286371 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286372 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286373 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286374 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286375 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1041 "selection" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286371 13194139534400 true] [17592186286370 1110 #uuid "5b3a4713-a4ec-5580-9fe2-79c0bbc9a91a" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286371 1034 "\\frac{y(2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y))}{x}" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286371 1111 #uuid "7f9d0166-6bec-5851-bb1c-43edcbc681ad" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286372 1034 "\\frac{2-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)}{xy}" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286372 1111 #uuid "22385bbd-e241-5b75-8da1-6b738f584e10" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286373 1034 "\\frac{2y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y)}{x}" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286373 1111 #uuid "fbeb15bd-6c98-5c6b-840a-b4a90fd4c2cc" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286374 1034 "\\frac{x(2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y))}{y}" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286374 1111 #uuid "9457067f-ebde-554e-aab5-df5dc4c93e14" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286375 1034 "\\frac{x(2y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y))}{y}" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286375 1111 #uuid "c301127b-8a8e-5745-b3ec-63b4d2a16958" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286376 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286377 13194139534400 true] [17592186286376 1089 "q-312258" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286376 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534400 true] [17592186286376 1100 "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(0,\\,0)$ for the curve ${x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4y=6x.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286376 1113 #uuid "f462b566-6d04-56f6-a1d4-dfc5ad7d21ad" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286376 1145 "To find the slope at a point, we use implicit differentiation to calculate the derivative of the curve, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\nNote that to differentiate the ${x}^{2}{y}^{3}$ term, we will need to use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4y & =6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}{y}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x) \\\\ [3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{y}^{3}]-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{y}^{3}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6-2x{y}^{3} \\\\ (3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6-2x{y}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{6-2x{y}^{3}}{3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at the point $(0,\\,0)$ is then given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}_{(0,\\,0)} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{6-2x{y}^{3}}{3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4})}_{(0,\\,0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-2\\cdot 0\\cdot {0}^{3}}{3\\cdot {0}^{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286378 13194139534400 true] [17592186286377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286379 13194139534400 true] [17592186286377 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534400 true] [17592186286377 1041 "field-1" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286377 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286378 13194139534400 true] [17592186286377 1110 #uuid "cfc616a9-6fee-5cfb-ab2e-7831a33a9f72" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286378 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286378 1111 #uuid "a969d92a-1eba-5894-8ba0-1e6b6abddb74" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286379 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286379 1111 #uuid "f8e55992-6baa-5167-90d7-9d4211d45add" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286380 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286381 13194139534400 true] [17592186286380 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286383 13194139534400 true] [17592186286380 1089 "q-342401" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286380 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534400 true] [17592186286380 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992403/assets/0c89b1d28ce7692f54e0fbf32c1d99b091e24729c837883523d6150450decb17.png)\n\nThe equation $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=20x$ represents an ellipse. The tangent line at the point $(4,4)$ on the ellipse intersects the $y$-axis at the point $P.$ What are the coordinates of $P?$\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286380 1113 #uuid "469198e0-64e7-505b-94c7-39658b9e1be1" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286380 1145 "First of all, we need to find the slope of the tangent line at the point $(4,4).$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we will calculate the derivative using implicit differentiation, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20x) \\\\ 8x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =20 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =20-8x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{20-8x}{2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{10-4x}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at the point $(4,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(4,\\,4)} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{10-4x}{y})|}_{(4,\\,4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-4\\cdot 4}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-6)}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can write the equation of the tangent at the point $(4,4)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4 & =-\\frac{3}{2}(x-4) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{2}(x-4)+4 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{2}x+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to find where this tangent line intersects the $y$-axis. At the point $P$ the $x$-coordinate is $0,$ so we set $x=0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{3}{2}x+10 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 0+10 \\\\ y & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,\\,10).$" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286382 13194139534400 true] [17592186286381 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534400 true] [17592186286381 1041 "field-1" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286381 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286382 13194139534400 true] [17592186286381 1110 #uuid "e6d53ad5-4ec5-5e16-8919-1fc595be6b13" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286382 1034 "0" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286382 1111 #uuid "b5d5ad37-a317-56c6-99a2-d30b41fd0a3d" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286383 1000 #edb/ref 17592186286384 13194139534400 true] [17592186286383 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534400 true] [17592186286383 1041 "field-2" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286383 1104 #edb/ref 17592186286384 13194139534400 true] [17592186286383 1110 #uuid "f0d0b1c5-893e-58d6-ab09-47e4d09ba084" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286384 1034 "10" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534400 true] [17592186286384 1111 #uuid "8f6ce041-9abc-5780-ad8c-e607d68b1ad8" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286385 1017 #edb/ref 17592186286386 13194139534400 true] [17592186286385 1089 "q-72214" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286385 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534400 true] [17592186286385 1100 "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $x{e}^{y}={x}^{2}.$" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286385 1113 #uuid "82be5ee4-1296-57ae-8b02-9dee15c642bb" 13194139534400 true] [17592186286385 1145 "First, we differentiate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\nNote that to differentiate the $x{e}^{y}$ term, we will need to use the product rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\t